holds no spec under active/<branch>/ (the closing move IS the signal). integrate_one: --no-ff --no-commit merge, trunk_step.py folded into the merge commit so it passes its own floor, check.py --jobs 0 at the declared tier on the composed tree read fail-closed (nonzero exit OR any SKIP line refuses), verdict gate per docs/process.toml [policies] review_rounds computed over the branch's own round files, restricted to a fresh full-lane round in either mode, or a final round only where reviewer retention is on and final_reviewer is persisted, whose scope runs from the lane's recorded claim base to the reviewed commit; a narrow round and a retained full round never admit. The gate is governed by TREE IDENTITY: a verdict counts only while it names the branch's current non-record tree at the work tip, so there is no ordering rule and no time comparison; an unreadable claim commit holds by name, a narrow-only lane never clears, and a phase whose latest round is invalid evidence holds by name as having no valid verdict; whether an adjudication lane owes a verdict at all is docs/process.toml [attestation] adjudication_review, read through the one function the loop's round scheduler also reads - over the same input, since which copy of a branch's spec answers for it when both the terminal and the active home carry one is decided by a single declared precedence (terminal first: it is what the closing session did) that both callers ask for rather than each walking the homes in its own order. The trailer is a cross-check over the newest attestation at the tree under judgement, refusing on a differing verdict word or a round count ABOVE the evidence and never on one below it - the attestation's writer is best-effort, so a stamp the evidence outruns is a missed stamp rather than a forgery, and understating cannot buy a merge the round files do not already buy. ff-only trunk advance, branch deleted on green, candidate parked on red. audit: git log --first-parent --no-merges over --since..HEAD; paths outside docs/work/, docs/log.d/, docs/log.md and the stack.ini [generated] set flag the commit. A missing stack.ini or an empty [product] test declaration refuses the merge; a red bar parks the candidate and stops the queue rather than composing past it.\"","+detail = \"claim: when the coordinator context guard is enabled and the claim does not hold the dispatch lock (the live dispatcher's route), a guard refusal comes first (no coordinator lease, a caller other than the lease holder, or a latched or threshold-crossing holder); then §2.3 steps 1+2 with the refusal ladder, cheapest first (tracked pause via agent_common.tracked_pause; an existing branch that is not an abandoned claim; an unsafe branch name; per claimed id, a queued spec that is not exactly one file with readable frontmatter, a SpecRef that does not resolve, or the id named in docs/status.md's hand prose; an id off the ready frontier) before anything is written. The trunk commit goes through bookkeeping.commit, under that helper's contract (IF-186) for isolation and install, scoped to the claim's own writes - each spec's link-aware move into active/<branch>/ and every file the move relinks, plus the regeneration's writes: a dirty path in that scope refuses by name before any step or checkout write, and the branch is cut before trunk advances. finished_branches: a claimed branch whose tip holds no spec under active/<branch>/ (the closing move IS the signal). integrate_one: --no-ff --no-commit merge, trunk_step.py folded into the merge commit so it passes its own floor, check.py --jobs 0 at the declared tier on the composed tree read fail-closed (nonzero exit OR any SKIP line refuses), verdict gate per docs/process.toml [policies] review_rounds computed over the branch's own round files, restricted to a fresh full-lane round in either mode, or a final round only where reviewer retention is on and final_reviewer is persisted, whose scope runs from the lane's recorded claim base to the reviewed commit; a narrow round and a retained full round never admit. The gate is governed by TREE IDENTITY: a verdict counts only while it names the branch's current non-record tree at the work tip, so there is no ordering rule and no time comparison; an unreadable claim commit holds by name, a narrow-only lane never clears, and a phase whose latest round is invalid evidence holds by name as having no valid verdict; whether an adjudication lane owes a verdict at all is docs/process.toml [attestation] adjudication_review, read through the one function the loop's round scheduler also reads - over the same input, since which copy of a branch's spec answers for it when both the terminal and the active home carry one is decided by a single declared precedence (terminal first: it is what the closing session did) that both callers ask for rather than each walking the homes in its own order. The trailer is a cross-check over the newest attestation at the tree under judgement, refusing on a differing verdict word or a round count ABOVE the evidence and never on one below it - the attestation's writer is best-effort, so a stamp the evidence outruns is a missed stamp rather than a forgery, and understating cannot buy a merge the round files do not already buy. ff-only trunk advance, branch deleted on green, candidate parked on red. audit: git log --first-parent --no-merges over --since..HEAD; paths outside docs/work/, docs/log.d/, docs/log.md and the stack.ini [generated] set flag the commit. A missing stack.ini or an empty [product] test declaration refuses the merge; a red bar parks the candidate and stops the queue rather than composing past it. The shared commit-floor refusal precedes even that first guard refusal and the dispatch lock.\""," rationale = \"\"\"One serial actor, one page; every refusal names its reason; the queue stops at the first red rather than composing past it.\"\"\""," test_refs = \"TC-132; TC-205; TC-331\""," status = \"Approved\""]},{"oldStart":3174,"oldLines":7,"newStart":3174,"newLines":7,"lines":[" title = \"Coordinator context occupancy, lease, and drain latch\""," module = \"project-trajectory/scripts/coordinator_guard.py;project-trajectory/scripts/integrate.py;project-trajectory/scripts/kitlib/shell_line.py\""," code_symbol = \"GuardConfig/guard_config/Occupancy/read_occupancy/lease_dir/take/release/clear/hand_back/record_event/latch_reading/window_refusal/claim_refusal/on_blackout/launch_reason/model_clis/command_name/command_words/_assigned/window_check/on_monitored/on_session_start/on_pre_compact/classify_compaction/hook;claim;segments/Unreadable/Word\"","-detail = \"guard_config reads the declared coordinator threshold and window: a non-positive, out-of-range or malformed threshold is off and a malformed window reads as the default. read_occupancy reads the newest valid assistant usage after the live transcript branch's latest compaction boundary, never a sidechain record, counting input and cached input; a record whose usage is malformed, partial or zero is skipped, and no valid usage reads as unknown, never zero. A primary-checkout lease names one coordinator session and its transcript. take refuses another holder; release frees the lease and clear unlatches it, each requiring and recording the owner's reason; hand_back accepts only the holder session and a handoff carrying a session prompt, frees the lease, and records the handoff; it refuses another or unnamed caller, whatever handoff it names, while naming the owner's release; it refuses the holder's own pending relaunch request, while a previous holder's request does not block it and is left for session_end's foreign-request refusal; with the guard off it returns before reading or writing. Elapsed time never transfers ownership. on_session_start installs a session as holder, unlatched, only when it presents the successor token the holder's exit wrote into the lease, and restates a latched drain to the holder's own resumed start. Only the holder's own hook payload on the holder's transcript is measured, never a subagent's. latch_reading latches drain when the unrounded reading reaches the threshold and retains it through lower readings, compaction and resume; it ends only through the owner's clear, the owner's release, the holder's hand-back, or a successor take. window_refusal runs before the dial on every claim route, including the dispatcher, naming the UTC end; the dispatcher remains exempt only from the context guard. claim_refusal identifies the claimant by the session id the agent CLI exports to its tool processes (CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID), refuses with no lease held or a claimant that is not the holder, and reads and latches the holder's transcript itself, so a refusal never depends on a hook having run; a claim holding the dispatch lock never calls it. While a window is armed hooks act at every dial and deny the closed list of the main session's Agent call, SendMessage call, Bash/PowerShell model-CLI command word, and a Bash/PowerShell line unreadable only because of an unclosed single quote, unclosed double quote, unclosed POSIX dollar quote, unclosed POSIX backtick substitution, unclosed dollar-parenthesis substitution, or unclosed PowerShell here-string. One quote-aware shell reading per dialect reads quoted values as the shell does, and treats quoted separators, comments and here-document and here-string bodies as data. It finds the model-CLI command word after leading variable assignments, the timeout and env prefixes, the shell's reserved words, the chain operators and the call operator, and in substitutions written in the line or inside double quotes. It reads a PowerShell assignment to a variable as running its right-hand command, while a quoted or variable right-hand value stays data. A form outside this list gets no dedicated recognition: it may incidentally match this reading, and carries no guarantee either way. window_check exits nonzero inside an armed window. At every SessionStart inside a window, hooks inject the blackout close-down instruction; each main session's monitored events inject it at that session's first monitored event in the window and every twentieth thereafter, counted per session per window: bring each open lane to its pause point, using a wrap-up adjudication for an active claim where needed; write the handoff naming each lane and its next obligation; request no relaunch; and end the session. Hook responses inject the latch instruction once and bounded reminders thereafter; inside a blackout window the latch is still recorded, but the blackout close-down, which requests no relaunch, is injected in its place. PreCompact records trigger, occupancy and latch/request state; classify_compaction reports missed-threshold, manual and during-drain cases. After identifying a session, the lease take first reads the guard hooks' state and records no holder unless it reads none or on, or a terminal consent installs them and the re-read reads on; without a terminal at absent, or at occupied, it refuses naming the consent step or the hooks to move.\"","+detail = \"guard_config reads the declared coordinator threshold and window: a non-positive, out-of-range or malformed threshold is off and a malformed window reads as the default. read_occupancy reads the newest valid assistant usage after the live transcript branch's latest compaction boundary, never a sidechain record, counting input and cached input; a record whose usage is malformed, partial or zero is skipped, and no valid usage reads as unknown, never zero. A primary-checkout lease names one coordinator session and its transcript. take refuses another holder; release frees the lease and clear unlatches it, each requiring and recording the owner's reason; hand_back accepts only the holder session and a handoff carrying a session prompt, frees the lease, and records the handoff; it refuses another or unnamed caller, whatever handoff it names, while naming the owner's release; it refuses the holder's own pending relaunch request, while a previous holder's request does not block it and is left for session_end's foreign-request refusal; with the guard off it returns before reading or writing. Elapsed time never transfers ownership. on_session_start installs a session as holder, unlatched, only when it presents the successor token the holder's exit wrote into the lease, and restates a latched drain to the holder's own resumed start. Only the holder's own hook payload on the holder's transcript is measured, never a subagent's. latch_reading latches drain when the unrounded reading reaches the threshold and retains it through lower readings, compaction and resume; it ends only through the owner's clear, the owner's release, the holder's hand-back, or a successor take. window_refusal runs before the dial on every claim route, including the dispatcher, naming the UTC end; the dispatcher remains exempt only from the context guard. claim_refusal identifies the claimant by the session id the agent CLI exports to its tool processes (CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID), refuses with no lease held or a claimant that is not the holder, and reads and latches the holder's transcript itself, so a refusal never depends on a hook having run; a claim holding the dispatch lock never calls it. While a window is armed hooks act at every dial and deny the closed list of the main session's Agent call, SendMessage call, Bash/PowerShell model-CLI command word, and a Bash/PowerShell line unreadable only because of an unclosed single quote, unclosed double quote, unclosed POSIX dollar quote, unclosed POSIX backtick substitution, unclosed dollar-parenthesis substitution, or unclosed PowerShell here-string. One quote-aware shell reading per dialect reads quoted values as the shell does, and treats quoted separators, comments and here-document and here-string bodies as data. It finds the model-CLI command word after leading variable assignments, the timeout and env prefixes, the shell's reserved words, the chain operators and the call operator, and in substitutions written in the line or inside double quotes. It reads a PowerShell assignment to a variable as running its right-hand command, while a quoted or variable right-hand value stays data. A form outside this list gets no dedicated recognition: it may incidentally match this reading, and carries no guarantee either way. window_check exits nonzero inside an armed window. At every SessionStart inside a window, hooks inject the blackout close-down instruction; each main session's monitored events inject it at that session's first monitored event in the window and every twentieth thereafter, counted per session per window: bring each open lane to its pause point, using a wrap-up adjudication for an active claim where needed; write the handoff naming each lane and its next obligation; request no relaunch; and end the session. Hook responses inject the latch instruction once and bounded reminders thereafter; inside a blackout window the latch is still recorded, but the blackout close-down, which requests no relaunch, is injected in its place. PreCompact records trigger, occupancy and latch/request state; classify_compaction reports missed-threshold, manual and during-drain cases. Before recording a holder, the lease take refuses an inactive commit floor and records no holder. After identifying a session, the lease take first reads the guard hooks' state and records no holder unless it reads none or on, or a terminal consent installs them and the re-read reads on; without a terminal at absent, or at occupied, it refuses naming the consent step or the hooks to move.\""," rationale = \"The context reading and lease are one admission fact: without one holder and a latched record, a tool-event observation can be missed and a later claim can start new work after the coordinator should be closing out.\""," test_refs = \"TC-315;TC-316;TC-317;TC-345\""," status = \"Approved\""]},{"oldStart":3481,"oldLines":3,"newStart":3481,"newLines":14,"lines":[" status = \"Approved\""," component = \"CMP-008\""," phase = 6","+[design.LLR-340]","+sr_refs = [\"SR-240\"]","+title = \"Commit-floor activation check and route refusal\"","+module = \"project-trajectory/scripts/kitlib/commit_hooks.py;project-trajectory/scripts/agent_loop.py;project-trajectory/scripts/session_service.py;project-trajectory/scripts/bookkeeping.py;project-trajectory/scripts/integrate.py;project-trajectory/scripts/coordinator_guard.py;scripts/coordinator/overnight_legs.py\"","+code_symbol = \"REQUIRED_HOOKS/hooks_refusal;HooksOffRefused/_refused_launch\"","+detail = \"For a checkout root, the commit-floor activation contract returns no refusal only when the resolved hooks directory is the checkout's or primary checkout's .githooks directory and both commit hooks can run; otherwise it returns a refusal naming the detected cause and its repair: activation for an unsuitable hooks path or unavailable Git answer, restoration for a missing hook, or executable-mode repair for an unrunnable hook. Each route applies that result before it creates route-specific work, and a session launch distinguishes this refusal from a blackout refusal.\"","+rationale = \"One checkout-level answer keeps every route from assigning a different meaning to an active commit floor. Refusal at each route boundary was selected over trusting callers because each boundary can begin governed work independently.\"","+test_refs = \"TC-370\"","+status = \"Drafted\"","+component = \"CMP-008\"","+phase = 6"]}]},{"filePath":"C:\\Projects\\ai-template.wt\\wi-926\\docs\\archive\\last_approved\\docs\\requirements\\system-requirements.toml","hunks":[{"oldStart":117,"oldLines":7,"newStart":117,"newLines":7,"lines":[" hat_refs = [\"SECURITY\"]"," requirement = \"\"\"The pre-commit hook shall run the integrity + secrets floor on every commit, agent-neutrally — a LOCAL floor, bypassable by the session (git commit --no-verify), so it discharges \"no unchecked write enters governed state\" only as a PAIR with the hosted re-run of the same bar (SR-151/SR-152), never alone.\"\"\""," rationale = \"\"\"Realizes SN-005 and SN-009 — a floor only CI enforces is one the local tree crosses freely, and a secret caught after the commit is already in history. Trusting the agent to run the checks was rejected: a floor exists for the times the agent forgets, so it is git-enforced and agent-neutral. Parents the interpreter probe: a hook that crashes cryptically because no python3 resolves, or because a Windows Store alias exits nonzero, has not run the floor — so probing by RUNNING a candidate and reporting clearly is machinery serving THIS obligation, and it decomposes to LLR-021 rather than standing as a requirement of its own.\"\"\"","-acceptance_criteria = \"The hook runs the registry-integrity floor and the secrets scan on staged content and blocks a commit that fails either. With no interpreter at the runtime floor, the commit hooks refuse the commit, name the developer-setup install step, and neither run the floor below that floor nor skip it. A --no-verify commit bypasses the hook and is caught instead by the hosted re-run, which is what makes the pair - not this row - the honest unit of the claim.\"","+acceptance_criteria = \"The hook runs the registry-integrity floor and the secrets scan on staged content and blocks a commit that fails either. With no interpreter at the runtime floor, the commit hooks refuse the commit, name the developer-setup install step, and neither run the floor below that floor nor skip it. A --no-verify commit bypasses the hook and is caught instead by the hosted re-run, which is what makes the pair - not this row - the honest unit of the claim. With no kit scripts directory, the commit hooks refuse the commit, name the repair, and neither run nor skip the floor.\""," priority = \"M\""," verification = \"Test\""," status = \"Approved\""]},{"oldStart":131,"oldLines":7,"newStart":131,"newLines":7,"lines":[" hat_refs = [\"DATA-PROTECTION\", \"SECURITY\"]"," requirement = \"\"\"The pre-push hook shall scan the outgoing commit range and block a push that publishes a secret or (under privacy-check) a private identity.\"\"\""," rationale = \"\"\"Realizes SN-005 and SN-009 — the last gate before content leaves the machine. Parents the interpreter probe, with SR-019: pre-push sources the shared probe declared by LLR-021, and a pre-push hook that cannot start scans nothing. The probe is mechanism, not a second obligation.\"\"\"","-acceptance_criteria = \"The hook scans the push range and blocks when a secret (always) or an identity/PII class (privacy-check on) appears. With no interpreter at the runtime floor, it refuses the push, names the developer-setup install step, and neither scans below that floor nor skips the scan.\"","+acceptance_criteria = \"The hook scans the push range and blocks when a secret (always) or an identity/PII class (privacy-check on) appears. With no interpreter at the runtime floor, it refuses the push, names the developer-setup install step, and neither scans below that floor nor skips the scan. With no kit scripts directory, the pre-push hook refuses the push, names the repair, and neither runs nor skips the scan.\""," priority = \"M\""," verification = \"Test\""," status = \"Approved\""]},{"oldStart":1887,"oldLines":3,"newStart":1887,"newLines":18,"lines":[" da_refs = [\"DA-017\"]"," aspect = \"unattended-loop\""," form = \"cross-cutting\"","+","+[requirement.SR-240]","+title = \"Commit-floor activation before agent routes\"","+sn_refs = [\"SN-005\"]","+boundary_refs = [\"B-01\", \"B-04\"]","+hat_refs = [\"SECURITY\"]","+requirement = \"Where a checkout's commit floor is inactive, the delivered agent routes shall refuse to start and name the applicable repair that activates the floor.\"","+rationale = \"A DERIVED requirement through the SECURITY lens: an agent route can create a governed commit, and an inactive commit floor leaves that action without the enforcement SN-005 expects. Start-time refusal was selected over a configurable bypass so the route cannot grant itself the authority the floor is meant to enforce.\"","+acceptance_criteria = \"Each route started in a checkout whose commit floor is inactive refuses before creating a lock, branch, commit, holder, log or session and names the applicable repair that activates the floor. With an active commit floor, each route starts normally. No external setting, flag or parameter disables the refusal.\"","+priority = \"M\"","+verification = \"Test\"","+status = \"Drafted\"","+phase = 6","+da_refs = [\"DA-004\"]","+form = \"cross-cutting\""]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["C:\\Projects\\ai-template.wt\\wi-926\\docs\\archive\\last_approved\\README.md","C:\\Projects\\ai-template.wt\\wi-926\\docs\\archive\\last_approved\\acts.toml","C:\\Projects\\ai-template.wt\\wi-926\\docs\\archive\\last_approved\\docs\\requirements\\low-level-requirements.toml","C:\\Projects\\ai-template.wt\\wi-926\\docs\\archive\\last_approved\\docs\\requirements\\system-requirements.toml"]}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01B94ZniqvnZ7vG2oL9ZUacL","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
